# Odyssey Gate — Week 14: The world works with others, and knows itself

**Concept:** GitHub/source control, pair programming, AI-aware coding
(`lessons/09-projects-tools-and-reflection.md`). **This week's gate is
Coding Odyssey Checkpoint 3 itself** — see
`assignments/A2-coding-odyssey-project.md` and `planning/week-14.md`. No
separate parallel gate. **Instruments:** Build (full) + **Full Trail
Debrief (mandatory)** — see `docs/curriculum/judgment_toolkit.md` §2/§4.

## Full Trail Debrief (mandatory this week — new, not in the original A2 template)

Weeks 12-13 were the deliberate refactor crisis: every major noun in your
world became a class. This Debrief is where you make that refactor's real
cost and payoff explicit, not just move past it. Answer specifically, not
in general terms:

1. **What broke** when you moved from dict/list entries to classes? Name a
   real bug or awkward moment, not "nothing, it went smoothly" (if it
   really did go smoothly, say what made it easy — that's useful evidence
   too, but be specific about why).
2. **Why** did it break — was it a design choice made back in Week 10-11
   that didn't anticipate objects, a Python mechanic you hadn't used before
   (`self`, mutation, references), or something else?
3. **What would you design differently**, starting from Week 1 with what
   you know now? This is the actual point of the Debrief — not
   self-criticism, evidence of a changed mental model.

This pairs with the already-scheduled Friday show-and-tell reflection tie-in
(`planning/week-14.md`, `assignments/A4-show-and-tell-reflection.md`) —
don't write two separate reflections; this Debrief *is* that week's
reflection, deepened.

## Optional side-quest: the world gets an advisor

This week's technical focus is literally "AI-aware coding practice" — the
natural home for calling an LLM API (Claude or similar) from inside your
project for one clearly-scoped task: summarizing your world's own log data,
classifying an event type, or generating a flavor-text description from
structured state. Not graded as a gate; genuinely optional enrichment.
Worth a line in your World Bible either way — even choosing not to attempt
it, with a reason, is a real judgment call.

## Professional-pathway portfolio update

This week already pairs with `assignments/A6-professional-pathway-artifacts.md`'s
mid-semester update (`planning/week-14.md`) — no change here, just a
reminder it's the same week.

## World Bible

Log the Debrief answers here — this is the mid-semester Judgment Log
touchpoint (`docs/curriculum/judgment_toolkit.md` §5).

