SalariedCommissionEmployee without using
inheritance, we could have copied class
CommissionEmployee’s code and pasted it into class
SalariedCommissionEmployee. Then we could have
modified the new class to include a base salary data attribute,
and the properties and methods that manipulate the base salary,
including a new earnings method. This copy-and-paste
approach is often error-prone. Worse yet, it can spread many
physical copies of the same code (including errors) throughout
a system, making your code less maintainable. Inheritance
enables us to “absorb” the features of a class without
duplicating code. Let’s see how.




