      In [3]: np.random.seed(11)

      In [4]: values = np.random.randint(10, 91, 10)

      In [5]: values
      Out[5]: array([35, 73, 90, 65, 23, 86, 43, 81,
      34, 58])



The following snippets call linear_search with the values
23 (found at index 4), 61 (not found) and 34 (found at index
8):


      In [6]: linear_search(values, 23)
      Out[6]: 4

      In [7]: linear_search(values, 61)
      Out[7]: -1

